                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Section</hi> 22, <hi rendition="#italic">chapter</hi>
                    71, <hi rendition="#italic">of the general statutes of Massachusetts of</hi>
                    1860.</head>
                <p>If the master or other person having charge of a vessel, therein brings to and
                    lands, or suffers to be landed, within this State, a person convicted in any
                    other State or in a foreign country, of an infamous crime, or a crime for which
                    he has been sentenced to transportation, knowing of such conviction, or having
                    reason to suspect it, or a person of a notoriously dissolute, infamous, and
                    abandoned life and character, knowing him to be such, he shall for every such
                    offense forfeit a sum not exceeding five hundred dollars.</p>
            </div>
